```
import { createAgent, createMiddleware, ToolMessage } from "langchain";

const handleToolErrors = createMiddleware({
  name: "HandleToolErrors",
  wrapToolCall: async (request, handler) => {
    try {
      return await handler(request);
    } catch (error) {
      return new ToolMessage({
        content: `Tool error: Please check your input and try again. (${error})`,
        tool_call_id: request.toolCall.id!,
      });
    }
  },
});

const agent = createAgent({
  model: "google-genai:gemini-3.5-flash",
  tools: [],
  middleware: [handleToolErrors],
});
```

### [​](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langchain/tools\#state-injection)  State injection

Tools can access the current graph state through [`ToolRuntime`](https://reference.langchain.com/javascript/langchain/index/Runtime):For more details on accessing state, context, and long-term memory from tools, see [Access context](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langchain/tools#access-context).

## [​](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langchain/tools\#prebuilt-tools)  Prebuilt tools

LangChain provides a large collection of prebuilt tools and toolkits for common tasks like web search, code interpretation, database access, and more. These ready-to-use tools can be directly integrated into your agents without writing custom code.See the [tools and toolkits](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/integrations/tools) integration page for a complete list of available tools organized by category.

## [​](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langchain/tools\#server-side-tool-use)  Server-side tool use

Some chat models feature built-in tools that are executed server-side by the model provider. These include capabilities like web search and code interpreters that don’t require you to define or host the tool logic.Refer to the individual [chat model integration pages](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/integrations/providers) and the [tool calling documentation](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/javascript/langchain/models#server-side-tool-use) for details on enabling and using these built-in tools.

